(Iron) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
( is an essential trace mineral element which forms an important component of hemoglobin\054) Tj
T*
(metallocompounds and Vitamin A\056 Deficiency of iron\054 leads to microcytic hypochromic anemia\056 The toxic) Tj
T*
(effects of iron are deposition of iron in various organs of the body and hemochromatosis\056) Tj
T*
/F2 9 Tf
(Total Iron Binding capacity \050TIBC\051) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
( is a direct measure of the protein Transferrin which transports iron from) Tj
T*
(the gut to storage sites in the bone marrow\056 In iron deficiency anemia\054 serum iron is reduced and TIBC) Tj
T*
(increases\056) Tj
T*
/F2 9 Tf
(Transferrin Saturation) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
( occurs in Idiopathic hemochromatosis and Transfusional hemosiderosis where no) Tj
T*
(unsaturated iron binding capacity is available for iron mobilization\056 Similar condition is seen in congenital) Tj
T*
(deficiency of Transferrin\056) Tj
